@startuml
title Output handling — File Output node support (flat-with-prefix)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Worker (vast / modal / community)" {
  [render_driver.py\n_patch_compositor_file_outputs()] as RD
  [Blender] as BL
  [IncrementalOutputUploader\n(top-level glob, unchanged)] as UP
}

package "/output/ filesystem (flat)" {
  folder "/output" as OUT {
    [Camera_frame0045.exr\n(main composite output)] as MAIN
    [<NodeName>_<SlotIdx>_frame0045.exr\n(File Output node files)] as SUB
  }
}

package "serverV2" {
  [POST /jobs/.../register-outputs] as API
  database "output_frames\n(group_id, filename,\n job_id, frame_number)" as DB
  [count_in_range()\nCOUNT(DISTINCT frame_number)] as Q
}

RD --> BL : 1. for each CompositorNodeOutputFile:\n   base_path = OUTPUT_DIR\n   slot.path = "<NodeName>_<idx>_frame"
BL --> MAIN : 2. main render output
BL --> SUB : 3. File Output nodes write here\n(unique prefix per node + slot)
UP --> MAIN : 4. existing top-level glob\n(no recursive walk needed)
UP --> SUB : 4.
UP --> API : 5. upload + register every filename
API --> DB : 6. INSERT (frame_number parses\nfrom "frame0045." in any name)
Q <-- DB : 7. completion stays filename-based,\nignores prefix differences

note bottom of RD
  Single change.  No upload, backend
  or DB schema edits required.
  Both renamings (base_path + slot.path)
  ensure every file has "frame####.ext"
  somewhere in its name so the
  ``frame(\\d+)\\.`` generated column matches.
end note

note bottom of UP
  Stays flat: ``os.listdir(/output)``.
  No subdir support needed.
end note
@enduml
